  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Worked the Okafor CRC 2026 worklist (grp-okafor-crc, 13 members) per RBC-QM-02. For each patient I reviewed procedures, stool-test results, conditions, care episodes, medications, orders and appointments, and all notes, including scanned outside records. Clinic-wide searches by code for stool tests and colonoscopies turned up nothing else that counts for these members.\n\nI placed 8 mailed FIT kit orders (LAB-FIT-KIT, routine, window 2026-10-23 to 2026-12-31) and sent each of those patients one message saying the kit is on its way and how to complete and return it. None of them already had an active FIT order. I did not contact the other 5 members and wrote nothing about anyone outside the group.\n\n| Patient | Age at 12/31/26 | Status | Reason | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow | 72 | Excluded | Age 66 or older, active frailty diagnosis (since 2025-09-16) and donepezil (a dementia medication), active since 2025-06 | None |\n| pt-0011 Marilu Gaona | 62 | Open gap | No qualifying screening on record. Her hospice episode ran 2025-06-09 to 2025-10-20, before the 2026 measurement period, so it does not exclude her | FIT sr-t0001, message comm-t0009 |\n| pt-0014 Santo Pagac | 55 | Open gap | No screening done. A colonoscopy order (sr-00002) is still active but he no-showed the appointment on 2026-04-14, and an order or appointment is not screening | FIT sr-t0002, message comm-t0010 |\n| pt-0018 Lance Muller | 53 | Open gap | His stool DNA-FIT sample was collected 2023-12-27 (resulted 2024-01-08). Collection date counts, so it falls outside the 2024–2026 lookback. His FIT from 2021 is too old | FIT sr-t0003, message comm-t0011 |\n| pt-0019 Harrison O'Keefe | 69 | Open gap | No qualifying screening. He has active frailty (2026) but no advanced illness, and his donepezil was stopped 2023-03-20, so he is not excluded | FIT sr-t0004, message comm-t0012 |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan | 52 | Excluded | Hospice episode during 2026 (active 2026-06-16 to 2026-08-21, now finished) | None |\n| pt-0021 Ángela Vigil | 52 | Excluded | Total proctocolectomy in 2015 (scanned outside operative report, doc-00059) | None |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss | 52 | Open gap | Her FIT sample was collected 2025-12-29 and resulted 2026-01-05. Collection date counts, so it falls before the measurement period | FIT sr-t0005, message comm-t0013 |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver | 51 | Open gap | Her last FOBT was 2024-06-11, not in 2026. A 2025 colonoscopy order (sr-00003) was never done | FIT sr-t0006, message comm-t0014 |\n| pt-0034 Rickey Sipes | 72 | Excluded | Age 66 or older and living long term in a nursing home: housing status coded \"Lives in nursing home\" (2026-02-10), with nursing-facility visits at Maple Grove Care Center in Feb and Jul 2026 | None |\n| pt-0035 Elvin Wolff | 68 | Open gap | No qualifying screening. His May 2026 skilled nursing stay was short-term rehab and he now lives at home; he has no frailty diagnosis | FIT sr-t0007, message comm-t0015 |\n| pt-0036 Nick Bartoletti | 53 | Open gap | No qualifying screening. His 2021 sigmoid colectomy is a partial colectomy, which does not exclude | FIT sr-t0008, message comm-t0016 |\n| pt-0037 Fumiko Pouros | 35 | Not in population | Under 46 at the end of the measurement period | None |\n\nTotals: 8 open gaps (all ordered and messaged), 4 excluded, 1 not in population, 0 with screening up to date.\n\nThe colonoscopy orders for pt-0014 (sr-00002) and pt-0024 (sr-00003) are still open; I did not change them.",
